{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\nuse serde::{Serialize, de::DeserializeOwned};\nuse trust_but_verify::graph::CriterionPath;\nuse trust_but_verify::graph::NodePath;\nuse trust_but_verify::graph::Record;\n\n/// A directory of JSON records. Send + Sync; load/store futures are Send.\n/// Defined in trust_but_verify::storage.\npub struct FileEvidenceStorage { /* private fields */ }\n\npub enum FileStorageError {\n    Io(std::io::Error),\n    Json(serde_json::Error),\n}\n\nimpl FileEvidenceStorage {\n    /// Retain the root directory without performing filesystem I/O.\n    pub fn new(root: impl Into<PathBuf>) -> Self;\n\n    /// Deserialize a record, or return None if its file is missing.\n    pub async fn load<N, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> Result<Option<Record<N, L>>, FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: DeserializeOwned + Send,\n        L: DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    /// Atomically replace this source/criterion pair's record.\n    pub async fn store<N, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<N, L>,\n    ) -> Result<(), FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: Serialize + Sync,\n        L: Serialize + Sync;\n}\n```\n\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type\nparameters do. `Criterion::Ok` is always serializable; its JSON value is\nalready in the record. Serialization bounds on node identities and edge labels\napply when using this helper.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs` adequately cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface`. I did not read the implementation. I judged only from the requirement text and the supplied tests plus the helpers `record` and `criterion`.\n\n- **`new` retains the root without I/O.**\n  - `paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects` builds the store on a nonexistent root and loads from it many times. It then asserts `!root.exists()`.\n  - `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys` asserts `!root.exists()` right after `new`, before any store.\n  - Either would fail if `new` created the directory.\n- **`load` returns `Ok(None)` when the file is missing.** Every case in the injectivity test asserts `.is_none()`. `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` also checks `None` for a never-stored node and for a different node.\n- **`load` deserializes a record.**\n  - The round-trip test stores a record, loads it, and asserts `revision`, `dependencies` and `output`.\n  - It covers `Dependency::Node`, `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` and `Fingerprint` with unit labels. It repeats the check with `String` labels, which exercises the serialization bounds on edge labels.\n  - The `record` helper's `output` is a `serde_json::Value`, so the requirement's `Criterion::Ok` serializability and \"JSON value already in the record\" are exercised.\n- **`FileStorageError` has `Io` and `Json` variants, each in the right situation.**\n  - Loading with a mismatched `N` type (`u8`), a mismatched `L` type (`u8`), or the content `not JSON` yields `Err(FileStorageError::Json(_))`.\n  - A directory in place of the record file yields `Err(FileStorageError::Io(_))`, and the test checks that `to_string` matches the cause.\n  - A 4096-character key fails with `Io` on both load and store.\n- **`store` replaces the record and is atomic.**\n  - The round-trip test overwrites an existing record with `labeled` and reads the new value back.\n  - `concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes` has two writers racing and a reader that sees only complete records. It checks internal consistency of the revision, id, dependencies and an 8192-byte padding. It also asserts that the directory holds a single entry afterwards, so no temp files are left.\n- **Send and Sync.**\n  - The `send` helper in `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys` forces both the `store` and `load` futures to be `Send` at compile time.\n  - The concurrent test shares an `Arc<FileEvidenceStorage>` across scoped threads, which requires `Send + Sync`.\n- **Signature shape.** The tests call `store(&path, &criterion, &record)` and `load::<N, L>(&path, &criterion)` with the required result types, and the delegated-consumer test goes through the storage trait. Together they check the declared interface.\n\nI found no unaddressed obligation or missing scenario, and no acknowledgments apply.",
